      text: "# Project Name: Credexa\n**Role:** Act as a Principal Web3 & AI Systems Architect and a Frontend UI/UX Expert.\n\n## Context & Vision\nCredexa is a decentralized invoice discounting and supply chain financing protocol designed for Indian MSMEs suffering from 90\342\200\223120 day payment delays by enterprise buyers[cite: 1]. The platform tokenizes verified invoices, secures funding via multi-tranche liquidity pools, and uses Gemini as an on-chain credit oracle[cite: 1]. All settlements and liquidity pool transactions are denominated in an INR-pegged stablecoin (e.g., eINR or a custom SPL INR token) to eliminate FX risk for local businesses.\n\n---\n\n## Technical & Design Specifications\n\n### 1. Solana Smart Contract Architecture (Anchor Framework)\nDesign and generate the Anchor (Rust) program structure, account schemas (PDAs), and instructions:\n* **Invoice Tokenization:** Mint verified invoices as SPL Token-2022 digital assets, utilizing metadata extensions to embed the legally binding debt assignment and invoice terms[cite: 1].\n* **Stablecoin Settlement:** Ensure all funding, repayments, and fee calculations strictly use an SPL-based INR-pegged stablecoin.\n* **Multi-Tranche Liquidity Pools:**\n  - **Junior Tranche:** High-yield, first-loss absorption pool for specialized underwriters[cite: 1].\n  - **Senior Tranche:** Protected, lower-yield pool for everyday liquidity providers (LPs)[cite: 1].\n  - Issue transferable SPL LP tokens to allow secondary market liquidity prior to invoice maturity[cite: 1].\n* **Default Handling & Factoring Modes:**\n  - **Recourse Factoring:** Automatic clawback logic that freezes/liquidates seller-staked collateral or intercepts future settlement distributions upon default[cite: 1].\n  - **Non-Recourse Factoring:** Protocol-absorbed default logic with higher risk premiums[cite: 1].\n* **Insurance Reserve Fund:** Route a configurable percentage of transaction fees into a Protocol Reserve PDA to buffer against catastrophic hard defaults[cite: 1].\n* **Grace Period & Default Trigger:** If an invoice remains unpaid 15 days past maturity, transition its on-chain status to `Defaulted`, transfer legal claims off-chain, and trigger an automated credit penalty for the defaulting party[cite: 1].\n* **Buyer Attestation & Rebates:** Create an instruction allowing enterprise buyers to co-sign/attest invoices with their keypair (lowering the discount rate), plus an automated rebate payout if they settle early[cite: 1].\n\n### 2. Gemini Multimodal Credit Oracle (Backend Pipeline)\nWrite a Python / Node.js backend integration using the Gemini Multimodal API:\n* **Document Audit:** Ingest and cross-examine multi-page Indian e-way bills, GST (GSTR-1/3B) filings, and enterprise Purchase Orders (POs)[cite: 1].\n* **Structured Output:** Return a strictly typed JSON payload containing an authenticity score, default risk tier, recommended discount rate, and underwriting flags[cite: 1].\n* **Oracle Signing:** Cryptographically sign the structured payload with an authorized Oracle keypair for verification inside the Anchor program.\n\n### 3. Compliance & Ecosystem Layer\n* **TReDS & GST Interoperability:** Model data schemas compatible with Indian TReDS platforms and exportable on-chain audit trails for GST tax compliance[cite: 1].\n* **Auto-Diversification Vaults:** Draft Anchor instruction outlines for depositing INR-pegged stablecoins into sector/geography-tagged pools[cite: 1].\n* **Notifications & UX:** Outline a webhook architecture to trigger WhatsApp/SMS updates on invoice funding status, payment deadlines, and auto-relisting triggers[cite: 1].\n\n### 4. Frontend & UI/UX Guidelines (Swiss Design)\nStructure the frontend framework (e.g., React, Next.js) using strict **Swiss Design (International Typographic Style)** principles to ensure trust, clarity, and ease of use for both MSMEs and DeFi Lenders:\n* **Grid System:** Employ a strict, asymmetric mathematical grid to organize complex financial data, liquidity pools, and invoice analytics[cite: 1].\n* **Typography:** Use highly legible, bold sans-serif typefaces (e.g., Helvetica, Inter, or Roboto). Rely on scale and weight for visual hierarchy rather than decorative elements. Use flush-left, ragged-right text alignment.\n* **Minimalism & Objectivity:** Remove all UI clutter. Prioritize raw data, clear actionable buttons, and straightforward navigation.\n* **Color Palette:** Utilize high-contrast, neutral backgrounds (whites, off-whites, and stark blacks) with highly deliberate, bold accent colors for critical status indicators (e.g., Green for Funded, Red for Defaulted).\n\n---\n\n## Expected Output\n1. Complete Anchor program layout (`lib.rs`, state structs, instruction handlers) utilizing Token-2022 and SPL token standards.\n2. Gemini multimodal prompt and Python audit pipeline returning signed credit payloads.\n3. Client-side interaction script demonstrating the end-to-end flow.\n4. A brief frontend component structure (React/Tailwind) demonstrating the Swiss Design implementation for the Analytics and Dashboard views."
    }
  }
}
