  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Key Requirements**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the user\'s requirements. Currently, my focus is on the Solana Smart Contract Architecture, specifically the Anchor framework. I need to make sure I fully design, architect, and generate a complete Anchor program. The goal is to ensure all four major sections and deliverables are fully addressed.\n\n\n**Defining Account Schemas**\n\nI\'ve moved on to meticulously crafting the account schemas for the Solana program, and have defined key data structures. The current focus centers around establishing `ProtocolConfig`, `InvoiceToken`, and the intricate design of the `LiquidityPool` / `TrancheVault`, which includes both `JuniorTranche` and `SeniorTranche` considerations and SPL LP tokens. The `InvoiceToken` structure encompasses detailed information on all of its state transitions. I\'m carefully considering all possible scenarios.\n\n\n**Expanding Default Strategies**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the default strategies, specifically concerning grace periods and trigger conditions. I\'m exploring the nuances of the `InsuranceReserve` PDA, and how it impacts hard defaults. I\'m also architecting a robust `BuyerAttestation` instruction, and its associated discount mechanisms. I\'m carefully determining how to incorporate an `AutoDiversificationVault` that considers sector and geography.\n\n\n**Constructing JSON Output**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in designing the structure of the JSON payload. This includes defining fields like `invoice_id`, `authenticity_score`, and `gst_reconciliation_status`, and the full architecture for `eway_bill_validity` along with an appropriate `default_risk_tier`. I\'m paying careful attention to `recommended_discount_rate_bps` and `max_advance_rate_pct`. I will also incorporate an `underwriting_flags` array, and a timestamp. Finally, I\'m working to cryptographically sign the output.\n\n\n**Designing Interoperability Systems**\n\nI\'m now integrating GST interoperability with TReDS factoring units and GSTR-1 records in an exportable JSON format to enhance the audit trail. I\'m also architecting the Auto-diversification vaults, creating an Anchor instruction outline and allocation algorithms across sectors and geographies. Finally, I\'m working to create a robust Webhook and Notifications architecture, including WhatsApp and SMS alerts for events like invoice funding, payment reminders, grace period notices, and defaults.\n\n**Constructing UI Guidelines**\n\nI\'m now fully focused on designing the Frontend UI/UX, adhering strictly to Swiss Design principles. I\'m implementing an asymmetric mathematical grid (24-col/12-col), high-contrast neutral palette and clear status accents. I\'m using Emerald Green for FUNDED/SETTLED, Crimson Red for DEFAULTED/DISCREPANCY, and Deep Cobalt Blue to cover status cues.\n\n\n**Refining UI Colors**\n\nI\'m now refining the UI colors, specifically for `GRACE_PERIOD` and `PENDING_ATTESTATION`, deciding on a Golden Amber shade. I\'m also planning flush-left ragged-right typography, tight proportional scales, and monospaced financial blocks. I\'m implementing a clean, tab-free multi-perspective architectural view to focus on the key requirements.\nI\'m designing Protocol Overview & Real-Time Macro Metrics, Invoice Exchange & Tokenization Engine, Gemini Multimodal Credit Oracle Sandbox and Multi-Tranche Liquidity Pools & eINR Vaults.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 156038757
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
