  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Frontend Guidelines**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the frontend and UI/UX guidelines, specifically how to implement a Swiss Design approach in the structure. I\'m considering React or Next.js to achieve trust and clarity. This design emphasizes principles like grid systems, a legible typography, and a clear hierarchy. I\'m aiming for a straightforward, intuitive user experience.\n\n\n**Designing Frontend Components**\n\nI\'m now structuring the frontend components. I\'ve designed `src/components/Header.tsx`, which incorporates the Swiss design principles. It features a bold brandmark, protocol stats, network indicator, active time display, and a perspective switcher. My plan is to emphasize clarity and directness, aligning with the core design ethos. I\'m focusing on simplicity, such as the use of an OVER perspective to reduce cognitive load. I\'m aiming for a straightforward user interaction.\n\n\n**Exploring New Module Designs**\n\nI\'m now diving into the design of core modules. I\'m exploring the `VIEW & ANALYTICS` section for macro metrics and cashflow analytics, as well as the `INVOICE EXCHANGE` with tokenized invoice listings. Next, I\'ll be working on `GEMINI CREDIT ORACLE`, auditing and crypto signatures. I\'m also planning to build the `MULTI-TRANCHE VAULTS` for varied risk profiles, and `BUYER CO-SIGN & REBATES` systems. Finally, `TReDS & ECOSYSTEM COMPLIANCE` and the `SOLANA CONTRACT SPEC` designs will be developed.\n\n\n**Analyzing Risk & Components**\n\nI\'ve been evaluating risk metrics, like senior/junior tranche TVL and default rates, and I\'m developing invoice component designs. I\'m building `InvoiceList.tsx`, a high-density, Swiss-styled data table, and `TokenizeModal.tsx` for new invoice tokenization. I\'m also planning an `OracleInspector.tsx` to test live API endpoints and structured data. I\'m focusing on features such as GSTIN validation.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 208889714
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
