  planner_response {
    response: "The **Anchor Rust Spec** tab is a built-in protocol reference and developer documentation viewer that displays the Solana smart contract source code that defines the on-chain logic for Credexa.\n\n### Why the code is displayed there:\n1. **On-Chain Protocol Transparency**: In Solana decentralized finance protocols, publishing the exact Anchor program source code (`lib.rs`, `state.rs`, `errors.rs`) allows institutional investors, underwriters, and smart contract auditors to review the exact rules governing funds \342\200\224 such as the 80/20 tranche waterfall, the 15-day default grace period, and the 200 bps buyer co-signing rebate.\n2. **Developer & Integration Reference**: It provides ready-to-use Anchor instructions and TypeScript SDK integration flows for developers connecting external ERPs (SAP, Tally) or institutional treasury systems to the protocol.\n\n---\n\n### Where to use the interactive application:\nIf you want to interact with the protocol instead of reading contract code, switch to the other tabs in the top navigation bar:\n- **Overview**: An interactive working capital simulator comparing traditional 90-day factoring delays against instant Solana liquidity.\n- **Invoice Exchange**: A live marketplace where you can tokenize receivables, submit invoices to the Gemini AI Credit Oracle, and view Token-2022 metadata.\n- **Tranche Vaults**: An investment portal for depositing capital into Senior (11.5% APY) and Junior (24.0% APY) risk pools.\n- **Buyer Attestation**: A portal for enterprise buyers (like Tata Motors or Reliance Retail) to review invoices, test pro-rata early settlement rebates, and co-sign.\n- **TReDS & Webhooks**: Integration tools for RBI-compliant TReDS registries and enterprise webhook testing.\n\n---\n\n### Options if you would like changes:\n- **Hide or remove the tab** if you want the navigation focused strictly on business and operational workflows.\n- **Replace it with an interactive contract explorer / transaction simulator** (e.g. visual PDA accounts, simulated transaction logs, and slot explorer).\n\nWould you like to keep this reference tab, hide it, or replace it with an interactive feature?"
    thinking: "**Defining the Context**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the context: the \"Anchor Rust Spec\" tab. I\'ve determined it\'s a built-in developer reference\342\200\224an audit tab, actually\342\200\224within the application, that provides the actual smart contract code, specifically `lib.rs`, `state.rs`, and `errors.rs` files, accessible via the `ContractSpecView.tsx` file.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "The **Anchor Rust Spec** tab is a built-in protocol reference and developer documentation viewer that displays the Solana smart contract source code that defines the on-chain logic for Credexa.\n\n### Why the code is displayed there:\n1. **On-Chain Protocol Transparency**: In Solana decentralized finance protocols, publishing the exact Anchor program source code (`lib.rs`, `state.rs`, `errors.rs`) allows institutional investors, underwriters, and smart contract auditors to review the exact rules governing funds \342\200\224 such as the 80/20 tranche waterfall, the 15-day default grace period, and the 200 bps buyer co-signing rebate.\n2. **Developer & Integration Reference**: It provides ready-to-use Anchor instructions and TypeScript SDK integration flows for developers connecting external ERPs (SAP, Tally) or institutional treasury systems to the protocol.\n\n---\n\n### Where to use the interactive application:\nIf you want to interact with the protocol instead of reading contract code, switch to the other tabs in the top navigation bar:\n- **Overview**: An interactive working capital simulator comparing traditional 90-day factoring delays against instant Solana liquidity.\n- **Invoice Exchange**: A live marketplace where you can tokenize receivables, submit invoices to the Gemini AI Credit Oracle, and view Token-2022 metadata.\n- **Tranche Vaults**: An investment portal for depositing capital into Senior (11.5% APY) and Junior (24.0% APY) risk pools.\n- **Buyer Attestation**: A portal for enterprise buyers (like Tata Motors or Reliance Retail) to review invoices, test pro-rata early settlement rebates, and co-sign.\n- **TReDS & Webhooks**: Integration tools for RBI-compliant TReDS registries and enterprise webhook testing.\n\n---\n\n### Options if you would like changes:\n- **Hide or remove the tab** if you want the navigation focused strictly on business and operational workflows.\n- **Replace it with an interactive contract explorer / transaction simulator** (e.g. visual PDA accounts, simulated transaction logs, and slot explorer).\n\nWould you like to keep this reference tab, hide it, or replace it with an interactive feature?"
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 899655482
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
